KG42.register("nodes-637f3db1e170a524efac640f",{"id":"KG31-e2bea6d6e2936fab","code":"OMC009.1","label":"Coordination of autonomous decisions guided by prices","definition":"The transaction price enters participants' autonomous supply, purchase, or energy-use decisions as revenue, cost, or a triggering condition; price evaluation, response feedback, and iteration apply only according to the source.","layer":"L4","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"coordination.price_signal","concept_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Decision authority: participants retain the choice over transactions or resource use","Input: the applicable transaction price and one's own economic conditions","Output: an autonomous supply quantity, a purchase choice, or an energy-use plan"]},"exclusions":[["The auctioneer publishes p_t; a selected RU chooses x_i^*=argmax_{0≤x_i≤b_i}[(p_t−r_i)x_i−α_i x_i²].","The single leader is the auctioneer, and the multiple followers are selected RUs; the auctioneer uses the supply response to evaluate SFC cost savings.","The RU parameters are the reservation price r_i, the sharing-willingness parameter α_i, and the shareable upper limit b_i; the price-strategy range is [p_t^min,p_t^max].","Source equation (11) is x_i^*=(p_t−r_i)/(2α_i); the capacity constraint in the bounded argmax is not removed on that basis.","Algorithm 1 traverses candidate prices and evaluates the responses; the time-varying case is applied time slot by time slot."],["The simplified strategy gives only the one-way trigger p_M \u003c p_i_max ⇒ buy_i = 1 and does not add the converse.","The maximum price limit differs by participant; the threshold strategy is only a simplified EMTS example.","Guiding demand-side management by variable prices is a general design possibility.","Price signals should convey information on energy scarcity or surplus; the platform provides local near-real-time market information."]],"members":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"70bc095c02578bf031b0d54ba69d5113bf40e26156d0d083a18baa255d2a6d9d","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003","node_id":"coordination.price_signal","function":"coordination.price_signal","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. | Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1. | Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. | Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. | Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g04-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"39afd20ea0ea72205a9a8a085e4da4716b0ead9015ac1c00c330d489bd6248a9","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005","node_id":"coordination.price_signal","function":"coordination.price_signal","unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit. Price signals should indicate energy scarcity or surplus. Scope: General microgrid market price-signal design.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. | General microgrid market price-signal design. | Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4b4dbcdf1deae944a3339a8f6be08b7f348f8d9de35c43da93d2800719bc6c35","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005","node_id":"coordination.price_signal","function":"coordination.price_signal","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction","24-brooklyn_microgrid"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. State-of-the-Art","anchor_text":"ge revenues for stakeholders [28], [29]. However, one similar- or- ity among most of the above menti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"the proposed modiﬁed auction scheme studied in Section IV 0) can be adopted in each time slot t = 1,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p12-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Case Study","anchor_text":"p gy y his have enough ES to share with the SFC. However, the ES to ed share in time slot 4 stems fr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}].","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"a lower net beneﬁt. Hence, Ui can be seen as a net beneﬁt ne to RU i for sharing its ES. The utility","equation_id":"(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"pt −ri x∗i = . (11) 2αi 7 Now, substituting the value of x∗i into (8) and performing some 8 simple a","equation_id":"(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved.","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["price_conditioned_autonomous_response","stackelberg_price_response_coordination"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG31-L4-SC-L4-34ee47d8e0b821e4","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L4","ontological_kind":"SC-L4-34ee47d8e0b821e4"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"The transaction price enters participants' autonomous supply, purchase, or energy-use decisions as revenue, cost, or a triggering condition; price evaluation, response feedback, and iteration apply only according to the source.","identity_fields":["Decision authority: participants retain the choice over transactions or resource use","Input: the applicable transaction price and one's own economic conditions","Output: an autonomous supply quantity, a purchase choice, or an energy-use plan"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.price_signal","source_occurrences":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"70bc095c02578bf031b0d54ba69d5113bf40e26156d0d083a18baa255d2a6d9d"},{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The auctioneer determines the price paid for sharing RU storage, with the stated objective of maximizing average SFC cost savings while satisfying their storage needs. Scope: Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction. The number of participating RUs identified by the determination rule informs determination of the auction price through the Stackelberg payment rule. Scope: Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. The determination rule selects the participating RUs and SFCs before the payment rule determines the auction price. Scope: Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. The auction-price strategy is restricted to [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] in the strategy-set and algorithm formulations. Scope: Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Auctioneer price determination in the community's modified storage-sharing auction. | Community storage-sharing Stackelberg payment rule as specified in the strategy-set definition and Algorithm 1. | Determination-rule participant selection and subsequent Stackelberg payment-rule pricing in the community storage-sharing auction. | Payment-rule price determination after participant selection in the base auction and in each time slot of its time-varying extension; this sequence does not cover the earlier determination of the upper price bound. | Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g04-e07"]},"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"39afd20ea0ea72205a9a8a085e4da4716b0ead9015ac1c00c330d489bd6248a9"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The auction price p_t announced by the auctioneer coordinates participating RUs' choices of ES space to share, with each RU choosing within [0, b_i] to maximize its own utility. Scope: The Stackelberg payment rule for joint ES sharing within the smart community, including its application within each time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E34"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. State-of-the-Art","anchor_text":"ge revenues for stakeholders [28], [29]. However, one similar- or- ity among most of the above menti","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this regard, considering the potential benefits of ES sharing, as discussed in [10], this paper investigates the case in which the SFCs in a smart community are allowed to share some fraction of the ESs owned by the RUs through a third party such as an auctioneer or a community representative."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E34","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"the proposed modiﬁed auction scheme studied in Section IV 0) can be adopted in each time slot t = 1,","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"To this end, for the modeled x_{i,t} ∀i ∈ N and q_{m,t} ∀m ∈ M, the proposed modified auction scheme studied in Section IV can be adopted in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T with a view to maximize (19) and (20) ∀t. It is important to note that the reservation price vector r_i of each RU i ∈ N and the bidding price vector a_m of each SFC m ∈ M can be modeled through any existing time-varying pricing schemes such as time-of-use price [3]. Now, p_t^* = [p_{t,1}^*, p_{t,2}^*, ..., p_{t,T}^*] and x^* = [x_1^*, x_2^*, ..., x_N^*] constitute the solutions of the proposed modified auction scheme in a time-varying condition, if the x^* comprises the solution vector of all ES spaces shared by the participating RUs in each time slot t = 1, 2, ..., T for the auction price vector p_t^*. Further, all the auction rules adopted in each time slot of the proposed time-varying case will be similar to the rules discussed in Section IV. Hence, the solution of the proposed modified auction scheme for a time-varying environment also possesses the incentive compatibility and individual rationality properties for each time slot."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each participating RU i, the ES amount x_i chosen in response to the announced price p_t lies in [0, b_i] and maximizes U_i(x_i) = (p_t - r_i)x_i - α_i x_i^2; equivalently, x_i^* is the argmax of that utility over 0 ≤ x_i ≤ b_i. Scope: Stackelberg price-signal coordination for participating RUs in the community ES-sharing auction; the time-varying extension applies the same per-slot response.","expression":"x_i^* = \\arg\\max_{0 \\le x_i \\le b_i} \\left[(p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2\\right]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R003-x-x_i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i","v141-c-R003-theta-b_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The auctioneer's announced price p_t is restricted to the interval [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], where p_t^{min} is the Vickrey price (second-highest reservation price) and p_t^{max} the highest reservation price for participating RUs. Scope: Stackelberg payment-rule price strategy in the community ES-sharing auction.","expression":"p_t \\in [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min","v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g01-E35"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"p p y y no participating agents in the auction mechanism will cheat once the payment and allocation ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We note that the intersection of the demand and supply curves demonstrates the highest reservation price $p_t^{\\max}$ for the participating $J - 1$ RUs. According to the Vickrey auction mechanism [14], the auction price for sharing the ES devices would be the second highest reservation price, i.e., the Vickrey price, which will be indicated as $p_t^{\\min}$ hereinafter."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Equation (11) reports the RU best response for a given price p_t as x_i^* = (p_t - r_i)/(2α_i). Scope: RU best response in the Stackelberg payment rule; the bounded argmax in C002 retains the source's [0, b_i] constraint.","expression":"x_i^* = \\frac{p_t - r_i}{2\\alpha_i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-p_t","v141-c-R003-x-x_i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E11"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Stackelberg coordination of RU decisions in response to the auctioneer's announced price facilitates determination of the storage-sharing auction price in the payment rule. Scope: Stackelberg payment rule for participating RUs and SFCs in the community storage-sharing auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g04-e07","v141-b-g02-E15"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E22","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Auction Based ES Ownership","anchor_text":"he rule, B) a payment rule and C) a storage allocation rule. Here, es the determination rule allows ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The payment rule enables the auctioneer to decide on the price that the customer needs to pay to the owners for sharing their ES devices, which allows the RUs to decide how much storage space they will be putting into the market to share with the SFCs. Finally, the auctioneer allocates the ES spaces for sharing to each SFC following the allocation rule of the proposed auction."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\Gamma = {{{1, 2, ..., J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {U_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, {X_i}_{i∈{1,2,...,J−1}}, Z, p_t}, (5) which consists of: i) the set of RUs {1, 2, ..., J −1} participating in the auction scheme and the auctioneer; ii) the utility U_i that each RU i reaps from choosing a suitable strategy x_i in response to the price p_t announced by the auctioneer; iii) the strategy set X_i of each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}; iv) the average cost savings Z incurred to each SFC m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K−1} from the strategy chosen by the auctioneer, and v) the strategy p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}] of the auctioneer."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p12-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Case Study","anchor_text":"p gy y his have enough ES to share with the SFC. However, the ES to ed share in time slot 4 stems fr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In this paper, we have modeled a modiﬁed auction based joint energy storage ownership scheme between a number of residential units (RUs) and shared facility controllers (SFCs). We have designed a system and discussed the determination, payment and allocation rule of the auction, where the payment rule of this scheme is facilitated by a single-leader-multiple-follower Stackelberg game (SLMFSG) between the auctioneer and the RUs. The properties of the auction scheme and the SLMFSG have been studied, and it has been shown that the proposed auction possesses the individual rationality and the incentive compatibility properties leveraged by the unique Stackeberg equilibrium of the SLMFSG. We have proposed an algorithm for the SLMFSG, which has been shown to be guaranteed to reach the SE and that also allows the auctioneer and the RUs to decide on the auction price as well as the amount of ES to be put into the market for joint ownership."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For a given auction price p_t, each participating RU i maximizes U_i(x_i) = (p_t − r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2 over 0 ≤ x_i ≤ b_i; the unique best response is x_i^*(p_t) = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i).","expression":"\\forall i \\in \\{1,\\ldots,J-1\\}: \\quad U_i(x_i) = (p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2, \\quad 0 \\le x_i \\le b_i; \\quad x_i^*(p_t) = \\arg\\max_{0 \\le x_i \\le b_i} \\left[ (p_t - r_i)x_i - \\alpha_i x_i^2 \\right] = \\frac{p_t - r_i}{2\\alpha_i}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p","v141-c-R005-x-xi"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-r","v141-c-R005-th-alpha","v141-c-R005-th-b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"as = {{{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, {Auctioneer}}, {Ui}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, {Xi}i∈{1,2,...,J−1}, Z, pt}, (5) wh","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Ui(xi) = (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi, (6) where, αi is the reluctance parameter of RU i, and ri is the reservation price set by RU i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"a lower net beneﬁt. Hence, Ui can be seen as a net beneﬁt ne to RU i for sharing its ES. The utility","equation_id":"(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In addition, the proposed utility function also possesses the following properties: i) the utility of any RU increases as the per unit price pt paid to it for sharing ES increases; ii) as the reluctance parameter αi increases, the RU i becomes more reluctant to share its ES, and consequently the utility decreases; and iii) for a particular price pt, the more an RU shares with the SFCs, the less interested it becomes in sharing more. To that end, for a particular price pt and reluctance parameter αi, the objective of RU i is max xi (pt −ri)xi −αixi^2, xi ≤bi. (7)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-C. Algorithm for Payment","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 7, NO. 3, MAY 2016 ny Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reac","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Algorithm for SLMFSG to Reach the SE 1: Initialization: p_t^* = p_t^{min}, Z^*=0. 2: for Auction price p_t from p_t^{min} to p_t^{max} do 3: for Each RU i ∈ {1, 2, ..., (J −1)} do 4: RU i adjusts its amount of ES x_i to share according to x_i^* = arg max_{0≤x_i≤b_i} [(p_t−r_i)x_i − α_i x_i^2]. (13) 5: end for 6: The auctioneer computes the average cost savings to SFCs Z = (Σ_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)/(K−1)) Σ_{i=1}^{J−1} x_i^*. (14) 7: if Z ≥ Z^* then 8: The auctioneer record the desirable price and maximum average cost savings p_t^* = p_t, Z^*=Z. (15) 9: end if 10: end for The SE (x^*, p_t^*) is achieved."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Substituting the RU best response into Z yields the unique auction price p_t^* that maximizes average SFC cost savings, given by equation (12).","expression":"p_t^* = \\frac{\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{1}{2\\alpha_i}\\right)\\left(\\sum_{m=1}^{K-1} a_m\\right) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{r_i(K-1)}{2\\alpha_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J-1} \\frac{K-1}{\\alpha_i}}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-p"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-th-a","v141-c-R005-th-r","v141-c-R005-th-alpha","v141-c-R005-th-K","v141-c-R005-th-J"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E15"],"ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"pt −ri x∗i = . (11) 2αi 7 Now, substituting the value of x∗i into (8) and performing some 8 simple a","equation_id":"(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, substituting the value of x_i^* into (8) and performing some simple arithmetic, the auction price p_t^* that maximizes the average cost savings to the SFCs can be found as p_t^* = \\frac{(\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{1}{2α_i})(\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1} a_m) + \\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{r_i(K−1)}{2α_i}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{J−1} \\frac{K−1}{α_i}}, (12) where a_m for any m ∈ {1, 2, ..., K −1} and α_i for any i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1} is exclusive. Therefore, p_t^* is unique for Γ, and thus Theorem 1 is proved."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"1468 δ2Ui \u003c 0. Hence, for any Alto xi, ∀i ∈{1, 2, . . . , J −1}, i.e., δx2i price pt ∈[pmint , pmaxt","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"δ^2U_i/δx_i^2 \u003c 0. Hence, for any xi, ∀i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, i.e., for any price p_t ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], each RU will have a unique x_i, which will be chosen from a bounded range [0, b_i] and maximize U_i. To this end, first we note that the amount of ES x_i^* at which the RU i achieves its maximum utility in response to a price p_t can be obtained from (6), x_i^* = (p_t − r_i)/(2α_i). (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-B. Payment Rule","anchor_text":"he Deﬁnition 1: Let us consider the game as described he in (5), where the utility of each RU i and ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Definition 1: Let us consider the game \\Gamma as described in (5), where the utility of each RU i and the average utility per SFC are described via U_i and Z respectively. Now, \\Gamma will reach an SE (x^*, p_t^*), if and only if the solution of the game satisfies the following set of conditions: U_i(x_i^*, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*) ≥ U_i(x_i, x_{-i}^*, p_t^*), \\forall i ∈ {1, 2, ..., J −1}, \\forall x_i ∈ X_i, p_t^* ∈ [p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}], (9) and \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t^*)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^* ≥ \\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{K−1}(a_m −p_t)}{K−1}\\sum_i x_i^*, (10) where x_{−i} = [x_1, x_2, ..., x_{i−1}, x_{i+1}, ..., x_{J−1}]."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-p_t","symbol":"p_t","meaning":"Auction price announced by the auctioneer as the price signal for sharing ES, per unit of energy in the source's Stackelberg payment rule.","kind":"operational","domain":"[p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g01-E36"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-p_t"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-x_i","symbol":"x_i","meaning":"Amount or fraction of ES space that RU i chooses to share in response to the announced auction price p_t.","kind":"operational","domain":"[0, b_i]","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g01-E12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-x_i"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-p","symbol":"p_t","meaning":"Auction price chosen by the auctioneer and paid by SFCs to RUs per unit of shared ES.","kind":"operational","domain":"[p_t^{min}, p_t^{max}]","unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-p"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-xi","symbol":"x_i","meaning":"Amount or fraction of ES space that RU i offers to share with SFCs in response to the auction price.","kind":"operational","domain":"[0, b_i]","unit":"energy (ES space; source uses ES space and energy interchangeably)","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-xi"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-r_i","symbol":"r_i","meaning":"Reservation price per unit of energy set by RU i; a fixed input to the RU's best response to the announced price p_t in this coordination stage.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"r_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-r_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i","symbol":"α_i","meaning":"Reluctance parameter of RU i measuring its unwillingness to share ES; a fixed coefficient in the RU utility used in the best response.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"α_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-alpha_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-b_i","symbol":"b_i","meaning":"Maximum shareable ES space of RU i, defined in the source as s_i^{cap} - d_i; it is the upper bound of the RU's ES-sharing strategy.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"s_i^{cap} - d_i"},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E17"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-b_i"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min","symbol":"p_t^{min}","meaning":"Lower bound on the auctioneer's price signal; identified in the source as the Vickrey price or second-highest reservation price for the participating RUs.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_t^{min} (Vickrey price)"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_min"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max","symbol":"p_t^{max}","meaning":"Upper bound on the auctioneer's price signal; identified in the source as the highest reservation price among the participating RUs at the supply-demand intersection.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_t^{max}"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-p_t_max"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-a","symbol":"a_m","meaning":"Reservation bid of SFC m: the maximum per-unit price SFC m is willing to pay for sharing ES with RUs.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-a"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-r","symbol":"r_i","meaning":"Reservation price of RU i per unit of energy.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-r"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-alpha","symbol":"\\alpha_i","meaning":"Reluctance parameter of RU i measuring its unwillingness to share ES.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-alpha"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-b","symbol":"b_i","meaning":"Maximum amount of battery/ES space that RU i can share, defined in the source as b_i = s_i^{cap} - d_i.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"energy (ES space)","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-b"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-K","symbol":"K","meaning":"Number of participating SFCs determined by the determination/matching rule; the pricing sums use K-1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-K"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-th-J","symbol":"J","meaning":"Number of participating RUs determined by the determination/matching rule; the pricing sums use J-1.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E32","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E18"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-th-J"}]},{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.price_signal","source_occurrences":[{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit. Price signals should indicate energy scarcity or surplus. Scope: General microgrid market price-signal design.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility. | General microgrid market price-signal design. | Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4b4dbcdf1deae944a3339a8f6be08b7f348f8d9de35c43da93d2800719bc6c35"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local market price information informs decentralized trading decisions, and EMTS may respond to variable prices through demand-side management. Scope: General microgrid EMTS design and the BMG virtual market's provision of local price information; demand-side management is a general design possibility.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06","v141-b-g02-e22"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the TransActive Grid private blockchain protocol (C3). Thus, the characteristics of data consistency, security, and verification are covered by the TransActive Grid platform and are inherited traits from the blockchain protocol. Based on measurements of demand and supply as well as market information, the platform tracks and displays local (near) real time energy prices on an intuitive interface. Thus, market participants may gather generation, consumption and market information, and trade energy needs accordingly. Trading is mostly done automatically by the EMTS (C6) and just requires several preferences of its market participants, e.g. the preferred energy sources and price limits."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"For the illustrative simple EMTS, the decentralized decision to buy energy on the microgrid market is triggered whenever the market price falls below its maximum price limit. Scope: Illustrative simple EMTS strategy in the general microgrid market design. Condition: The microgrid market price falls below the EMTS's maximum price limit.","expression":"p_M \u003c p_i_max => buy_i = 1","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta001","v141-c-R005-theta002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e06","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.6 Energy management trading system (EMTS) (C6)","anchor_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EMTS’s main objective is to automatically secure the energy supply for a market participant while implementing a specific bidding strategy. The EMTS needs access to the (real time) demand and supply data of its market participant. Based on this data the EMTS forecasts consumption and generation, and develops its bidding strategy accordingly. Furthermore, it trades the predicted amounts on the market platform and may react to variable prices via demand side management [53]. Self-interested rational market participants maximize their revenue and minimize their energy costs. A simple EMTS would always buy energy at the microgrid market when the price falls below its maximum price limit. However, individual agents’ intelligent bidding strategies shall employ varying prices at different times and are one of the core components of active local markets."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Price signals should indicate energy scarcity or surplus. Scope: General microgrid market price-signal design.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x001","symbol":"buy_i","meaning":"Decentralized purchase decision of EMTS/market participant i for the illustrative simple EMTS strategy; 1 denotes buying energy on the microgrid market and 0 denotes not buying. The source describes the action but provides no explicit mathematical symbol.","kind":"operational","domain":"binary {0,1}; formalized purchase action, source gives no explicit notation","unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x001"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta001","symbol":"p_M","meaning":"Microgrid local market energy price observed by the EMTS when applying the simple buying rule; descriptive symbol because the supplied text gives no explicit notation.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta001"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta002","symbol":"p_i_max","meaning":"Maximum price limit of EMTS/market participant i for buying energy on the microgrid market; descriptive symbol because the supplied text gives no explicit notation.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e06"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","stage":"L4","subtype":"stackelberg_price_response_coordination","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The auctioneer publishes the price p_t, and the RU accordingly chooses x_i^*=argmax_{0≤x_i≤b_i}[(p_t−r_i)x_i−α_i x_i²]; the auctioneer uses the supply response to evaluate SFC cost savings and coordinates the price and shared-quantity decisions.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the price setter and the participants who autonomously choose the supply quantity","Core relationship: a price is published, participants make a best response in utility, and the organizer evaluates the price from the response","Output: interrelated price and supply decisions"],"variation_fields":["The single leader is the auctioneer, and the multiple followers are selected RUs","The RU parameters include the reservation price r_i, the sharing-willingness parameter α_i, and the shareable upper limit b_i","The price-strategy range is [p_t^min,p_t^max]","Source equation (11) is additionally retained: x_i^*=(p_t−r_i)/(2α_i); the capacity constraint in the bounded argmax is not removed on that basis","Algorithm 1 traverses candidate prices and evaluates the responses; the time-varying case is applied time slot by time slot"],"constraint_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"paper_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.price_signal","template_code":"DA"},{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","stage":"L4","subtype":"price_conditioned_autonomous_response","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The EMTS autonomously makes a transaction response on the basis of the local price; the simplified strategy gives the one-way trigger p_M \u003c p_i_max ⇒ buy_i = 1. Variable prices may also guide demand-side management, and price signals should convey information on energy scarcity or surplus.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the market price observed by the entity and the purchase response","Relationship: a purchase is triggered when the price is below the entity's maximum limit price","Output: autonomous purchase decision buy_i"],"variation_fields":["The maximum price limit varies by participant.","The threshold strategy is only a simplified EMTS example.","Demand-side management is a general design possibility.","The platform provides local near-real-time market information."],"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C003"],"paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.price_signal","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","retained_variants":["The auctioneer publishes p_t; a selected RU chooses x_i^*=argmax_{0≤x_i≤b_i}[(p_t−r_i)x_i−α_i x_i²].","The single leader is the auctioneer, and the multiple followers are selected RUs; the auctioneer uses the supply response to evaluate SFC cost savings.","The RU parameters are the reservation price r_i, the sharing-willingness parameter α_i, and the shareable upper limit b_i; the price-strategy range is [p_t^min,p_t^max].","Source equation (11) is x_i^*=(p_t−r_i)/(2α_i); the capacity constraint in the bounded argmax is not removed on that basis.","Algorithm 1 traverses candidate prices and evaluates the responses; the time-varying case is applied time slot by time slot."],"evidence_refs":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal::projection"]},{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","retained_variants":["The simplified strategy gives only the one-way trigger p_M \u003c p_i_max ⇒ buy_i = 1 and does not add the converse.","The maximum price limit differs by participant; the threshold strategy is only a simplified EMTS example.","Guiding demand-side management by variable prices is a general design possibility.","Price signals should convey information on energy scarcity or surplus; the platform provides local near-real-time market information."],"evidence_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-fee30c9c873061f6","baseline_parent_code":"OMC009","secondary_class":"SC-L4-34ee47d8e0b821e4","category":{"id":"SC-L4-34ee47d8e0b821e4","stage":"L4","label_zh":"Price-guided autonomous trading and energy-use decisions.","definition_zh":"Applicable transaction prices enter participant decisions as costs, revenues, or trigger conditions, and participants autonomously choose supply, purchase, exchange, or energy-use plans; price publication, response return, and update cycles are limited by the source.","main_identity_axes":["Decision authority: participants retain the right to choose trading or energy use.","Input-action relationship: prices enter individual economic decisions.","Output: autonomous trading choices, quantities, or operating plans."],"inclusion_criteria":["Explicitly specify how prices enter autonomous trading or energy-use decisions.","Threshold response, local optimization, or a feedback process including price updates may be used.","Sources need not share the same price formation, publication, or iteration procedure."],"exclusion_criteria":["The coordinator directly issues device operation control commands.","The main function is bid revision through matching feedback or cost pass-through across market bids.","The main function is feedback on inconsistency in bilateral contract selection or updating consistency variables.","Only price information is provided, and no autonomous response relationship is established."],"supporting_unit_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","04-energy_collectives::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-a-M02::coordination.price_signal","02-dlmp::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"The transaction price enters participants' autonomous supply, purchase, or energy-use decisions as revenue, cost, or a triggering condition; price evaluation, response feedback, and iteration apply only according to the source.","identity_fields":["Decision authority: participants retain the choice over transactions or resource use","Input: the applicable transaction price and one's own economic conditions","Output: an autonomous supply quantity, a purchase choice, or an energy-use plan"],"member_unit_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/331"});
